.\" Companion overview manpage for go-rs.
.\" Contact https://github.com/MenkeTechnologies/go-rs to correct errors or omissions.
.TH GOALL 1 "2026-07-23" "go-rs 0.1.3" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
goall \- go-rs overview: architecture, language surface, and toolchain
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B go-rs
is a pure Go frontend for the
.B fusevm
bytecode VM. The pipeline is
.IR "lexer \(-> parser \(-> compiler \(-> fusevm::Chunk" ,
after which fusevm runs the chunk on its three\-tier Cranelift JIT. No component
interprets Go directly; there is no Go runtime and no garbage collector \(em
goroutines ride fusevm's own cooperative scheduler.
.SH ARCHITECTURE
.TP
.B lexer.rs
Hand\-written lexer implementing Go's automatic semicolon insertion (ASI).
.TP
.B parser.rs
Recursive\-descent parser building a Go AST.
.TP
.B compiler.rs
Lowers the AST to fusevm ops; tracks a static numeric type so
.B int / int
truncates while
.B float / float
stays exact, and dispatches string
.B +
and ordering through the fusevm numeric hook.
.TP
.B host.rs
The
.B fmt
print family and builtin
.BR println / print ,
the heap backing slices/arrays/maps/structs, the
.BR strings / strconv / math / sort / os
builtins, plus the inline\-Rust FFI compile/call builtins.
.TP
.B pkg.rs
Resolves a non\-native
.B import
to real Go source, name\-qualifies it, and links it into the same compilation
unit (with
.B stdlib_vendor.rs
supplying the packages vendored into the binary).
.TP
.B aot_native.rs
Drives
.BR "go build" :
fusevm's ahead\-of\-time object emitter, linked against the go\-rs runtime
.RB ( libgors.a )
into a standalone native executable.
.TP
.BR lsp.rs " / " dap.rs
The
.BR \-\-lsp " / " \-\-dap
servers, and the documentation corpus behind
.B go doc
and
.BR docs/reference.html .
.SH LANGUAGE SURFACE
A
.B package main
entry file plus imported packages linked from source; top\-level
.B func
and methods with parameters, results, and recursion;
.BR ":=" " / " var ,
assignment (parallel and multi\-value) and compound assignment;
.BR if / else ,
.BR switch ,
type switch, the three\-clause / condition / infinite / range
.BR for ,
and
.BR break / continue / return ;
arithmetic, the full bitwise set, comparisons, and short\-circuit
.BR "&&" " / " "||" ;
.BR struct s
with methods and pointers, interfaces with dynamic dispatch, slices, fixed\-size
arrays, maps, channels with
.BR select ,
closures capturing by reference,
.BR defer / panic / recover ,
and erased generics;
.BR fmt / strings / strconv / math / sort / os
as native builtins. Open gaps: fixed\-width integer wrapping (all integers are
64\-bit), monomorphized generics, and source packages that reach
.BR unsafe / cgo / reflect
or assembly.
.SH TOOLCHAIN
Standalone
.B go
binary;
.BR \-\-lsp " / " \-\-dap
servers over stdio; a
.B _go
zsh completion; this man page and
.BR go (1);
an HTML docs/report site with a generated
.BR reference.html ;
inline
.B rust {}
FFI;
.B go doc
offline reference lookup; and
.BR \-\-dump\-tokens " / " \-\-dump\-ast " / " \-\-disasm " / " \-\-tiers
introspection.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR go (1)
